ADDITIONAL NOTE ON DATA, NOT LICENCE

This licence covers the source code only. The system processes personal data
about identifiable individuals — students and lecturers — and that processing
is governed by Ghana's Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843), not by this file.

Two consequences that a deployer is responsible for, both described in
docs/SECURITY.md:

  1. The demo accounts created by `db/seed.sql`
     (admin@utas.edu.gh, lecturer@utas.edu.gh, student@utas.edu.gh) exist for
     evaluation only. Their passwords are in the breach-password list used by
     the password policy, and Config::assertProductionSafe() refuses to treat
     them as production credentials. They must not exist in a production
     database.

  2. `users` rows carry a `deleted_at` soft delete precisely so that a record
     is not physically destroyed while a subject's right of access persists.
     Right-of-access requests are handled as a documented operational process
     (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §10), not as a DELETE.
